@startuml Weaver Validation Flow

!define PASS_COLOR #2ECC71
!define FAIL_COLOR #E74C3C
!define WEAVER_COLOR #3498DB

title Weaver Live-Check Validation Flow (The Only Source of Truth)

participant "Developer" as Dev
participant "clnrm CLI" as CLI
participant "Test Engine" as Engine
participant "Container" as Container
participant "OTLP Exporter" as OTLP
participant "Weaver Live-Check" as Weaver
participant "Schema Registry" as Registry
participant "CI/CD" as CI

== Schema-First Development ==

Dev -> Registry : 1. Define telemetry schema
activate Registry
note right
  test_execution.yaml:
    span.clnrm.test_execution:
      attributes:
        - container.id: required
        - test.isolated: boolean
        - test.result: enum
end note

Dev -> Weaver : 2. weaver registry check
Weaver -> Registry : validate schema
Weaver --> Dev : schema valid ✓
deactivate Registry

Dev -> Weaver : 3. weaver registry generate rust
Weaver -> Registry : load schema
Weaver --> Dev : type-safe builders generated
note right
  TestExecutionSpan::new(
    container_id,
    test_name
  )
end note

== Test Execution with Live Validation ==

Dev -> CLI : 4. clnrm run tests/ --validate

activate CLI
CLI -> Weaver : start live-check listener
activate Weaver
note right of Weaver #WEAVER_COLOR
  weaver registry live-check
  --otlp-grpc-port 4317
  --registry registry/
end note

CLI -> Engine : execute tests
activate Engine

loop For each test
  Engine -> Container : create isolated container
  activate Container

  Engine -> Container : execute test steps
  Container --> Engine : test results

  Engine -> OTLP : export telemetry
  activate OTLP
  note right
    Span: test_execution
      container.id: "abc123"
      test.isolated: true
      test.result: "pass"
  end note

  OTLP -> Weaver : stream telemetry

  Weaver -> Registry : load schema for validation
  activate Registry

  Weaver -> Weaver : validate telemetry\nagainst schema

  alt Telemetry Matches Schema
    Weaver --> OTLP : ✓ validation passed #PASS_COLOR
    note right of Weaver #PASS_COLOR
      **TRUE POSITIVE**

      Telemetry proves:
      - Container ran (container.id exists)
      - Isolation worked (test.isolated = true)
      - Test executed (test.result = pass)

      Feature is VALIDATED ✓
    end note
  else Telemetry Doesn't Match Schema
    Weaver --> OTLP : ✗ validation failed #FAIL_COLOR
    note right of Weaver #FAIL_COLOR
      **VALIDATION FAILURE**

      Missing required attribute:
        container.id

      This means:
      - Container may not have run
      - Feature is NOT working
      - MUST FIX before shipping
    end note
  end

  deactivate Registry
  deactivate OTLP
  deactivate Container
end

Engine --> CLI : all tests completed
deactivate Engine

Weaver -> Weaver : generate validation report
Weaver --> CLI : validation results

alt All Validations Passed
  CLI --> Dev : ✓ Tests passed\n✓ Telemetry validated #PASS_COLOR
  note right
    Exit code: 0

    Safe to ship!
    Feature proven to work.
  end note
else Any Validation Failed
  CLI --> Dev : ✗ Tests passed\n✗ Telemetry validation FAILED #FAIL_COLOR
  note right
    Exit code: 1

    DO NOT SHIP!
    Tests may have false positives.
    Fix telemetry or implementation.
  end note
end

deactivate CLI
deactivate Weaver

== CI/CD Integration ==

CI -> CLI : clnrm run tests/ --validate

alt Weaver Validation Passes
  CLI --> CI : exit 0 #PASS_COLOR
  CI -> CI : build passes
  CI -> CI : deploy
else Weaver Validation Fails
  CLI --> CI : exit 1 #FAIL_COLOR
  CI -> CI : build FAILS
  note right
    CI blocks deployment
    until Weaver validation passes
  end note
end

== The Critical Difference ==

note over Dev, CI #FFEB9C
  **Traditional Testing (What We Replace)**

  cargo test → All tests pass ✓
  └─ Ship it!
  └─ Risk: Tests can have false positives

  **Weaver Validation (What We Use)**

  weaver registry live-check → Telemetry validated ✓
  └─ Ship it!
  └─ Proof: Runtime behavior matches schema

  **Key Insight:**
  Tests validate test code.
  Schemas validate production behavior.
end note

@enduml
